  "text": "Count the jumps between the marks, not the marks. This one is tricky. Want an easier one?",
  "source": "exercise-note-easier-offer"
 },
 {
  "key": "4ef8b06aa522ab8b",
  "text": "Owl says: the 7s are the trickiest, and you already know most of them! Hedgie has two tricks: anything times 0 is 0, and anything times 1 stays the same.",
  "source": "lesson-story"
 },
 {
  "key": "505c71eccfcc70b2",
  "text": "You add 2. Now it's 8.",
  "source": "race-you-add"
 },
 {
  "key": "50bf363dae1e648e",
  "text": "You add 1. Now it's 4.",
  "source": "race-you-add"
 },
 {
  "key": "510c7804c482d755",
  "text": "Owl says: a double adds a number to itself, and half is one of two equal parts. Hedgie uses doubles to help: 35 plus 36 is double 35 and 1 more. To halve, split the tens and the ones!",
  "source": "lesson-story"
 },
